// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6234 Add macOS rule for sensitive data archived via ditto
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6234
// Pull request author: clivoa
// Change: new rule
// Title: Sensitive Data Archived Via Ditto - MacOS
// Sigma ID: 7b1f4c62-9e83-4a51-bb27-6d0c3e5a8f14
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: clivoa
// Date: 2026-08-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: collection, T1560.001, T1005
// Description: Detects the "ditto" utility creating an archive from a path that holds credentials, browser
//   secrets or cryptocurrency wallet data. "ditto" is Apple's own copy and archive tool and
//   preserves resource forks and extended attributes, which makes it a convenient way to package
//   collected data into a single archive before exfiltration. The "/Cookies" value covers both the
//   Chromium "Cookies" database and the "Library/Cookies" folder that holds Safari's
//   "Cookies.binarycookies". Plain copies are not matched, because a copy into one of these paths,
//   such as restoring SSH keys, would otherwise alert. Infostealers such as AMOS archive a staging
//   folder that they filled beforehand, so their archive command line does not contain these paths
//   and is not covered by this rule.
// False positives:
//   - Backup or migration tooling that archives the Keychain directory or SSH keys on a schedule
//   - A user archiving their own SSH keys or browser profile before moving to another machine
// References:
//   - https://www.loobins.io/binaries/ditto/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/f59f330f51734bd85b5e14dcb3af5e98f424fe6a/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_sensitive_data_archived_via_ditto.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/ditto" and ProcessCommandLine matches regex "\\s-[jkvVXz]*c[jkvVXz]*\\s" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/.ssh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/Cookies" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/Electrum" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/Exodus" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/Ledger Live" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/Library/Keychains" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Extension Settings" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Login Data")
